cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, you must cite the peer-reviewed article listed under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "City2Graph: A Python Library for Heterogeneous Graph Neural Networks and Spatial Analysis in Urban Systems"
abstract: "Any use of City2Graph in research must cite the peer-reviewed article: Sato, Y., Pietrostefani, E., Mahabir, R., & Arribas-Bel, D. (2026). City2Graph: A Python library for Heterogeneous Graph Neural Networks and spatial analysis in urban systems. Computers, Environment and Urban Systems, 130, 102492 (https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compenvurbsys.2026.102492). City2Graph is a Python library that provides an integrated interface of geospatial datasets from multiple domains converting into graph representations. It facilitates the one-stop data pipeline for spatial network analysis and Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) for GeoAI applications."
